KG42.register("rules-d252e160ceba40b7b3db7f34",{"id":"40-fair_dso_flexibility::v141-c-R002","paper":"40-fair_dso_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R002","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The DSO may acquire flexibility services from asset aggregators to maintain network voltages and currents within safe limits. Scope: Proposed distribution-system flexibility market for asset aggregators. The DSO is responsible for operating the distribution system so that voltage and current magnitudes remain within safe limits. Scope: DSO responsibility for operating the distribution system served by the flexibility market.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"DSO responsibility for operating the distribution system served by the flexibility market. | Proposed distribution-system flexibility market for asset aggregators.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E28"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"V_sqr","symbol":"V^{sqr}_{i,t}","meaning":"Squared voltage magnitude at node i in period t.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative real","unit":"kV^2","indices":["i ∈ Ω_b","t ∈ Ω_T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E33","v141-b-g01-E29"]},{"variable_id":"I_sqr","symbol":"I^{sqr}_{ij,t}","meaning":"Squared current magnitude on line ij in period t.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative real","unit":"A^2","indices":["ij ∈ Ω_l","t ∈ Ω_T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E33","v141-b-g01-E29"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"V_min","symbol":"\\underline V","meaning":"Minimum voltage magnitude.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kV","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E32","v141-b-g01-E29"]},{"parameter_id":"V_max","symbol":"\\overline V","meaning":"Maximum voltage magnitude.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kV","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E32","v141-b-g01-E29"]},{"parameter_id":"I_max","symbol":"\\overline I_{ij}","meaning":"Maximum current magnitude for line ij.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"A","indices":["ij ∈ Ω_l"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E32","v141-b-g01-E29"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The DSO may acquire flexibility services from asset aggregators to maintain network voltages and currents within safe limits. Scope: Proposed distribution-system flexibility market for asset aggregators.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The DSO is responsible for operating the distribution system so that voltage and current magnitudes remain within safe limits. Scope: DSO responsibility for operating the distribution system served by the flexibility market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E28"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The DSO's safe-operation responsibility for voltage and current magnitudes is expressed by the source's nodal voltage and line-current bounds: squared voltage magnitude lies between the squared minimum and maximum voltage limits at every node and period, and squared current magnitude lies between zero and the squared maximum line current at every line and period.","expression":"\\underline{V}^{2} \\le V^{sqr}_{i,t} \\le \\overline{V}^{2}, \\quad \\forall i\\in\\Omega_b, t\\in\\Omega_T; \\quad 0 \\le I^{sqr}_{ij,t} \\le \\overline{I}_{ij}^{2}, \\quad \\forall ij\\in\\Omega_l, t\\in\\Omega_T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["V_sqr","I_sqr"],"parameter_refs":["V_min","V_max","I_max"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E32","v141-b-g01-E33"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-7a81b1c717-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"Abstract—The proliferation of distributed energy assets neces- sitates the provision of ﬂexibility t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Abstract—The proliferation of distributed energy assets necessitates the provision of flexibility to efficiently operate modern distribution systems. In this article, we propose a flexibility market through which the DSO may acquire flexibility services from asset aggregators in order to maintain network voltages and currents within safe limits. A max-min fair formulation is proposed for the allocation of flexibility. Since the DSO is not aware of each aggregator’s local flexibility costs, we show that strategic misreporting can lead to severe loss of efficiency. Using mechanism design theory, we provide a mechanism that makes it a payoff-maximizing strategy for each aggregator to make truthful bids to the flexibility market. While typical truthful mechanisms only work when the objective is the maximization of Social Welfare, the proposed mechanism lets the DSO achieve incentive compatibility and optimality for the max-min fairness objective."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E28","location":{"location_id":"src-7a81b1c717-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"SO FLEXIBILITY MARKETS 2251 n- the day-ahead market and it is communicated by the day-ahead ant mark","equation_id":"(1)-(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The DSO is responsible for the operation of the distribution system, so that voltage and current magnitudes remain within safe limits. For this purpose, the DSO draws on the flexibility offered by the aggregators in \\(\\Omega_b\\), that is, the ability of an aggregator to modify its active power demand \\(P^D_{i,t}\\) at timeslot \\(t\\) by a certain factor \\(K_{i,t}\\). A modification \\(K_{i,t}P^D_{i,t}\\), results in an active power injection \\(P^S_{i,t}\\), determined by the active power balance equation \\(\\sum_{ki\\in\\Omega_l}P_{ki,t}-\\sum_{ij\\in\\Omega_l}(P_{ij,t}+R_{ij}I^{sqr}_{ij,t})+P^S_{i,t}=K_{i,t}P^D_{i,t},\\quad\\forall i\\in\\Omega_b,t\\in\\Omega_T\\quad (1)\\). The corresponding reactive power flows are represented as \\(\\sum_{ki\\in\\Omega_l}Q_{ki,t}-\\sum_{ij\\in\\Omega_l}(Q_{ij,t}+X_{ij}I^{sqr}_{ij,t})+Q^S_{i,t}=K_{i,t}Q^D_{i,t},\\quad\\forall i\\in\\Omega_b,t\\in\\Omega_T\\quad (2)\\). Notice that aggregators are assumed to maintain a constant power factor and also, it is assumed \\(P^S_{i,t}=Q^S_{i,t}=0\\) for all buses but the substation. On the other hand, for the substation bus, notice that \\(P^S_{0,t}\\) can also be less than 0, representing back-feeding. It should be noted that these assumptions are without loss of generality with respect to the methods that will be presented."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E29","location":{"location_id":"src-7a81b1c717-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"presented. Since current and voltage magnitudes appear naturally as hat squared, non-negative, conti","equation_id":"(3)-(7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Since current and voltage magnitudes appear naturally as squared, non-negative, continuous variables in the steady-state operation of AC electrical distribution systems, it is convenient to perform the change in variables \\(V^{sqr}_{i,t}\\equiv V_{i,t}^2\\) and \\(I^{sqr}_{ij,t}\\equiv I_{ij,t}^2\\) as in [35]. The voltage magnitude drop between nodes \\(i\\) and \\(j\\) is represented by \\(V^{sqr}_{i,t}-2(R_{ij}P_{ij,t}+X_{ij}Q_{ij,t})-(R_{ij}^2+X_{ij}^2)I^{sqr}_{ij,t}=V^{sqr}_{j,t},\\quad\\forall ij\\in\\Omega_l,t\\in\\Omega_T\\quad (3)\\), while current magnitudes are calculated using \\(V^{sqr}_{j,t}I^{sqr}_{ij,t}=P_{ij,t}^2+Q_{ij,t}^2,\\quad\\forall ij\\in\\Omega_l,t\\in\\Omega_T\\quad (4)\\). Upper and lower bounds on nodal voltage magnitudes and current magnitudes are enforced by \\(\\underline V^2\\le V^{sqr}_{i,t}\\le\\overline V^2,\\quad\\forall i\\in\\Omega_b,t\\in\\Omega_T\\quad (5)\\) and \\(0\\le I^{sqr}_{ij,t}\\le\\overline I_{ij}^2,\\quad\\forall ij\\in\\Omega_l,t\\in\\Omega_T\\quad (6)\\). An aggregator’s flexibility is bounded as in \\(\\underline K_{i,t}\\le K_{i,t}\\le\\overline K_{i,t},\\quad\\forall i\\in\\Omega_b,t\\in\\Omega_T\\quad (7)\\)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E32","location":{"location_id":"src-7a81b1c717-p01-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"NOMENCLATURE","anchor_text":"NOMENCLATURE Sets A er b Set of nodes/aggregators. Fl l Set of lines. tow T Set of time periods. ati","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Sets: \\(\\Omega_b\\) Set of nodes/aggregators. \\(\\Omega_l\\) Set of lines. \\(\\Omega_T\\) Set of time periods. Parameters: \\(\\lambda_{i,t}\\) Parameter of flexibility cost at node i, period t [$/kWh^2]. \\(\\overline K_{i,t}\\) Maximum flexibility factor at node i, period t. \\(\\underline K_{i,t}\\) Minimum flexibility factor at node i, period t. \\(\\overline I_{ij}\\) Maximum current magnitude for line ij [A]. \\(P^D_{i,t}\\) Active power demand at node i, period t [kW]. \\(Q^D_{i,t}\\) Reactive power demand at node i, period t [kvar]. \\(R_{ij}\\) Resistance of line ij [m\\Omega]. \\(\\overline V\\) Maximum voltage magnitude [kV]. \\(\\underline V\\) Minimum voltage magnitude [kV]. \\(X_{ij}\\) Reactance of line ij [m\\Omega]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E33","location":{"location_id":"src-7a81b1c717-p01-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"NOMENCLATURE","anchor_text":"es- V Maximum voltage magnitude [kV]. rn V Minimum voltage magnitude [kV]. ar- Xij Reactance of line","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Variables: \\(K_{i,t}\\) Flexibility factor at node i, period t. \\(I^{sqr}_{ij,t}\\) Squared current magnitude at line ij, period t [A^2]. \\(P_{ij,t}\\) Active power flow at line ij, period t [kW]. \\(P^S_{i,t}\\) Active power injection at substation i, period t [kW]. \\(Q_{ij,t}\\) Reactive power flow at line ij, period t [kvar]. \\(Q^S_{i,t}\\) Reactive power injection at substation i, period t [kvar]. \\(V^{sqr}_{i,t}\\) Squared voltage magnitude at node i, period t [kV^2]."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-activation","v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","quote":"In this article, we propose a flexibility market through which the DSO may acquire flexibility services from asset aggregators in order to maintain network voltages and currents within safe limits."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E28","quote":"The DSO is responsible for the operation of the distribution system, so that voltage and current magnitudes remain within safe limits."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"18d2e1d55f6e984bc4bd80c61916380f76bbe31a5a27f1ffc48714b87dc148ad","applicability":"formalized","reason":"C001 and C002 are retained as procedural coordination constraints. C002's safe-operation responsibility is additionally formalized by the source's voltage and current magnitude bounds (5)-(6), attached to the only frozen node coordination.local_operator. C001's permission to acquire flexibility remains procedural because the frozen graph has no clearing.local edge and the source gives no standalone formula for a bare permission. B evidence remains unreviewed under the experiment policy.","bindings":[{"object_id":"V_sqr","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Squared voltage magnitude is the operational voltage state used in the source's safe-limit bounds (5); in this rule it is attached to the DSO's local safe-operation responsibility. No edge exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"I_sqr","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Squared current magnitude is the operational line-current state used in the source's safe-limit bounds (6); in this rule it is attached to the DSO's local safe-operation responsibility. No edge exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"V_min","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The minimum voltage magnitude parameter enters the source's lower voltage bound (5), which supports the DSO's safe-operation responsibility. No edge exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"V_max","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The maximum voltage magnitude parameter enters the source's upper voltage bound (5), which supports the DSO's safe-operation responsibility. No edge exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"I_max","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The maximum line current magnitude parameter enters the source's current bound (6), which supports the DSO's safe-operation responsibility. No edge exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 formalizes the DSO's safe-operation responsibility stated in C002 using source equations (5)-(6). It is attached to the only frozen coordination node because no other node or edge is available in this rule."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
